{"id": "EUVD-2026-65528", "enisaUuid": "dde1aff1-f93a-3870-9ee6-1463fb884823", "description": "Nokogiri versions before 1.19.3 contain regular expression denial of service vulnerabilities in the CSS selector tokenizer affecting string-literal and identifier tokenization. Attackers can inject adversarial CSS selectors into methods like Node#css, Node#at_css, and Searchable#search to cause exponential regex backtracking and denial of service.", "datePublished": "2026-08-25T15:16:03", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-16T15:51:27", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/sparklemotion/nokogiri/security/advisories/GHSA-c4rq-3m3g-8wgx", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/nokogiri-before-redos-via-css-selector-tokenizer"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5jhf-fpp7-v2pv", "CVE-2026-79770"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.49, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "5c638892-01e5-320c-b8b2-a6089d1eb0a8", "product": {"name": "nokogiri", "vendor": {"name": "sparklemotion"}}, "product_version": "0 <1.19.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a0565297-d5a3-3616-bc44-ee862967af5e", "vendor": {"name": "sparklemotion"}}], "isExploited": false}